  "subject": "an old man in Tsuen Wan who, every winter solstice eve, hand-rolls black-sesame tong yuen, two each, for his three grown children's households and grandkids coming for dinner, keeps miscounting, ends up three over, then needs four more when his son brings his girlfriend's mother and his son-in-law wants four, and gives his own bowl to his grandson",
  "caption": "Cantonese bluegrass, acoustic string-band bluegrass sung in Cantonese. Rolling three-finger five-string banjo, a sawing fiddle, flatpicked acoustic guitar runs, slapped upright bass, mandolin chop on the backbeat. Dry acoustic string-band room sound, close mics, no drums. Male weathered mid-range voice with plain storytelling delivery and a gang-vocal chorus. 128 BPM, G major. Fussy, folksy and laughing. No drum kit, no country-pop gloss, no trap, no autotune, no electric guitar.",
  "lyrics": "[Verse]\n冬至前一晚 我喺荃灣屋企\n一包糯米粉 一碗黑芝麻\n大仔一家四個 二女一家三\n細仔帶埋女朋友 再加我同老婆\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n搓好一粒 擺落個盤\n口度數住 一 二 三\n\n[Chorus]\n數錯湯圓 數錯湯圓\n一人兩粒 點解又唔夠數\n數錯湯圓 數錯湯圓\n阿爺我 再搓多兩粒\n\n[Verse]\n孫女坐喺我隔籬 話幫阿爺數\n數到十七 就攞咗一粒去搓公仔\n我又試咗一粒 驚啲餡唔夠甜\n試完先記得 嗰粒係二女嘅\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n重新排過 一家一行\n大仔行頭 細仔排最尾\n\n[Chorus]\n數錯湯圓 數錯湯圓\n十一個人 點解有廿五粒\n數錯湯圓 數錯湯圓\n多出嗰三粒 唔知係邊個嘅\n\n[Verse]\n冬至夜晚 成屋都係人\n細仔入門 話女朋友帶埋佢阿媽\n二女個老公 又話要食四粒\n老婆喺廚房 笑住叫我再開粉\n\n[Bridge]\n多出三粒 都仲爭一粒\n我自己嗰碗 就讓返畀個孫\n\n[Chorus]\n數錯湯圓 數錯湯圓\n今晚個個 都話食得好飽\n數錯湯圓 數錯湯圓\n聽年冬至 我再數過\n\n[Outro]\n數錯湯圓\n一 二 三 四 數到天光",
